{
  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "Evidence: Our best result (config_018, acc=0.619) uses pca_n2000 as the RNA encoder in a multimodal, multiprofile, avgpool, concat setup. All completed experiments have used only PCA as the RNA encoder, leaving the learned-encoder dimension (scvi_n200, scgpt) completely unexplored. Question: config_030 is a clean single-variable change from config_018, swapping pca_n2000 → scvi_n200 while holding multimodal, multiprofile, resnet50, avgpool, and concat fixed. This directly tests whether a nonlinear, biologically-informed learned encoder outperforms linear PCA in the multimodal fusion context. Why this is the best next experiment: The RNA encoder is a fundamental architectural choice with potentially large upside—if scvi captures richer cell-type structure than PCA, the gain would transfer to all downstream multimodal configurations. Conversely, if it does not improve over PCA, we can confidently rule out learned encoders and concentrate remaining budget on image-encoder and fusion-strategy variations. Compared to testing weighted fusion (config_019), which is a more incremental change with likely smaller effect size, the encoder choice carries higher information value per experiment under a limited budget."
}

